{
  "id": "iron-bridge",
  "title": "Iron Bridge",
  "theatre": "Joint · plains / riverine estuary",
  "summary": "A dawn river crossing has failed. Three BLUE elements must converge on IRON BRIDGE and seize a bridgehead before hostile engineers drop it. UAV and ground sensors disagree about hostile armour, a jammer isolates one platoon, a C2 outage hits mid-fight, and air support only arrives if the ALO asks for it.",
  "durationMin": 30,
  "defaultSeed": 2611,
  "brief": {
    "situation": "BLUE Brigade's dawn crossing at the IRON BRIDGE site failed under observed fire. The bridge (E5) is still standing but prepared for demolition by hostile engineers on the south bank (E6). HHQ INTSUM: a hostile armour company is assessed in the D6–E7 area; decoy employment is likely. A hostile EW detachment has been active east of the crossing. A coastal patrol vessel (OPV ARGUS) is watching the estuary to the east.",
    "mission": "KESTREL Company seizes IRON BRIDGE intact and establishes a bridgehead at E6 by T+20 in order to enable BLUE Brigade's crossing at T+25.",
    "execution": "Three elements converge: KESTREL 1 (PL A) from the west, KESTREL 2 (PL B) from the east, Company HQ follows on the axis C2–D4. HAWK 1 (ALO) controls the UAV and can request close air support (available from T+15 if requested). SPECTRE (EW) manages the PACE plan and the rebro on HILL 214 (D3). TRIDENT (NLO) exploits the coastal radar and naval reporting.",
    "sustainment": "Runners available at every HQ. Casualty evacuation via C2.",
    "command": "PACE: CMD NET → alternate net → HF NET → RUNNER. If cut off from KESTREL 6, act on the commander's intent."
  },
  "terrain": [
